The best result so far is 13,119 cycles, which input-stationary on 32x8 and output-stationary on 8x32 both hit exactly. That looks like a memory-transfer floor. I'll use one more call to check whether the floor depends on array shape: output-stationary on 16x16. Its compute should be about 32 column folds × ~174 cycles ≈ 5,600, which is still well under 13,119. If this run also lands at 13,119, the floor does not depend on shape, and I'll submit one of the 13,119 designs.

